```python
lisa_transitions(
    data,
    variable,
    first=None,
    last=None,
    *,
    w=None,
    permutations=999,
    seed=12345,
    alpha=0.05,
    tiles='carto-positron',
    title=None,
    gdf=None,
    ref=None,
)
```

Transitions between local Moran (LISA) types: did the hot spots and cold spots persist?

Runs ``lisa`` in two years on the same units and the same weights, and counts how
the units moved between the types High-High, Low-High, Low-Low, High-Low and
Not significant.

## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}

| Name         | Type        | Description                                                                                                    | Default            |
|--------------|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------|
| data         |             | A dataset id, or a panel with ``geo_id`` and ``year``, e.g. from ``load``                                      | _required_         |
| variable     | str         | The numeric column to analyse                                                                                  | _required_         |
| first        |             | The two years to compare (default: the first and last with data); only the units with a value in both are used | `None`             |
| last         |             | The two years to compare (default: the first and last with data); only the units with a value in both are used | `None`             |
| w            |             | Spatial weights from ``weights`` (default: queen contiguity among the units with data)                         | `None`             |
| permutations | int         | Random permutations behind each unit's pseudo p-value                                                          | `999`              |
| seed         | int \| None | Makes the permutations reproducible                                                                            | `12345`            |
| alpha        | float       | Significance level below which a unit is assigned to a cluster                                                 | `0.05`             |
| tiles        | str \| None | The basemap style of the map (``None``: no basemap)                                                            | `'carto-positron'` |
| title        | str \| None | The title of the matrix figure                                                                                 | `None`             |
| gdf          |             | Boundaries to use instead of the project's (a GeoDataFrame with ``geo_id``)                                    | `None`             |

## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}

| Name   | Type          | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
|--------|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | result object | A result with ``.df`` (one row per unit: ``cluster_<first>``, ``cluster_<last>``, ``moved`` and the ``transition`` in words), ``.matrix`` (units by type in the first year, rows, and in the last year, columns; always the five types, in the same order), ``.shares`` (each row as shares of its total; empty rows are missing), ``.fig`` (the matrix as a heatmap: counts in the cells, coloured by the share of the row), ``.fig_map`` (the types in the last year, with the units that changed type outlined), ``.n_units``, ``.n_stayed``, ``.n_moved``, ``.share_stayed``, the global Moran's I of each year (``.moran_i_first``, ``.moran_i_last``, with ``.p_sim_first`` and ``.p_sim_last``) and ``.interpret()``. |

## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}

```python
!pip install -q geo4bolivia
import geo4bolivia as geo

res = geo.lisa_transitions("sdg", "index_sdg")       # ~2012 to ~2024
print(res.interpret())
res.fig
```

